<title>USA: US House Banking panel democrats seek rate hearing.</title>
<headline>US House Banking panel democrats seek rate hearing.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>All but three of the 24 Democrats on the House Banking Committee have asked the panel's chairman to hold a hearing on the Federal Reserve's recent action to raise interest rates.</p>
<p>In a letter to Iowa Republican and Chairman Jim Leach released Wednesday, the group led by Reps. John LaFalce of New York and Barney Frank of Massachusetts, said the recent Fed move &quot;may have been an unnecessary and unwise increase...&quot;</p>
<p>They added that the Fed's action &quot;seems to fly in the face of economic data indicating that inflation is not a near-term threat.&quot;</p>
</text>
